<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanva dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 75–<a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kanva dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> after the Shungas, traditionally for forty-five years in the first century BCE. Its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasudeva-kanva">Vasudeva Kanva</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> minister, killed the last Shunga king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devabhuti">Devabhuti</a>, and the dynasty had four kings. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a> it was ended by an Andhra king, often identified with the Satavahanas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanva-dynasty.jpg" alt="Kanva dynasty" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lessman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_in_50_bc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
